From e102d3474b74d18d50cd151f224ab55ff5e71151 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wang xinxiang <wxinxiang8@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 17:29:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 31/44] phy: rockchip-samsung-dcphy: fix shared state and power
 rollback

The TX and RX PHYs share hardware state but are independently
reference-counted by the PHY core. Reading peer->power_count under
the provider mutex races with updates protected by each PHY's own
mutex. Keeping lanes and HS rates in the parent also lets one
direction overwrite the configuration of the other.

Store configuration per direction and track active directions under
the provider mutex. Reject invalid lane/rate requests and conflicting
PHY types, and round RX rates up when selecting the settle settings.

Unwind RX lanes and TX reset/PLL state when power-on fails. Propagate
the reset and PLL failures handled by these paths so unsuccessful
transitions do not mark a direction active.

Signed-off-by: wang xinxiang <wxinxiang8@gmail.com>
---
